 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration{{% available_from "v1.151.0" %}} allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-servers).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway availability zone to discover instances from, e.g. "fr-par-1" (mandatory).
+    #
+  - zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # project_id is an optional Scaleway project id to filter instances by.
+    #
+    # project_id: "..."
+
+    # server is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # server: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Scaleway API requires a secret key for authentication, which can be passed via
+    # the `headers` HTTP API client option below, e.g. `headers: ["X-Auth-Token: <secret-key>"]`.
+    #
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the instance if it has one, or its private IPv4 address otherwise, while `<port>` is the port
+specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the status of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone of the instance, e.g. `fr-par-1`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_region`: the region of the instance, e.g. `fr-par`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_arch`: the architecture of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the project id of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the organization id of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public IPv6 of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the instance.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
